message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: GeoSocialX
abstract: >-
  A Python package for the geospatial analysis of geotagged social and location
  data. It reads geotagged records from CSV, GeoJSON, Bluesky (AT Protocol), or
  the X (Twitter) API into a common record type, then computes coverage
  statistics, spatial hotspots, and temporal trends, and exports GeoJSON and
  interactive maps. The analysis core uses only the Python standard library, and
  it reports honest exact-vs-place-vs-no-geo coverage so that the sparsity of
  geotagged social data is made explicit rather than silently ignored.
